WEBVTT

00:00:02.970 --> 00:00:08.350
Will I miss seeing the tower
before I come back to Kyoto?

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:10.320
Yajiro-niichan!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.650
I'm sorry we're late, Yajiro.

00:00:13.650 --> 00:00:16.220
I couldn't find Mother.

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:17.530
That's fine.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:21.310
What if Mother tried to keep me from going?

00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:23.290
I wouldn't be able to leave.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.250
Well, you might be right.

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:30.170
Your mother must really
not like seeing people off.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:34.450
Yajiro-niichan, do you have your medicine?

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.640
Yeah, I have it right here.

00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.240
Don't forget to take it.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.050
You'll turn back into a frog.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:44.600
So, where are you going first?

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:46.500
Well...

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:52.010
First, I think I'm going to visit the tanuki
that live in Komachi Onsen in Kurashiki.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:56.860
I'll think about the rest
while I'm on the road.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:01.070
I heard that my brother asked
that you visit our branch family.

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.300
I humbly thank you.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.870
If you happen to go to Shikoku,

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:08.330
make sure you say hello to Kincho clan.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:09.710
Got it.

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.670
Now, you're all set.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:18.600
I'm sure it'll be a great trip, Yajiro-kun.

00:01:19.150 --> 00:01:20.370
Thanks.

00:01:20.810 --> 00:01:24.640
You'll officially be my big sister
by the time I come back, Gyokuran.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.900
Why do you have to mention that now?

00:01:30.300 --> 00:01:33.480
Thank you for properly seeing me off.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:38.000
I, Shimogamo Yajiro, hope to return
from this journey

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.870
a bigger man than I am now.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:44.820
Please take care.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.600
You can come back any time.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:48.860
We'll be waiting for you.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:50.270
Yeah, we will.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:52.130
Bring home some souvenirs.

00:01:52.630 --> 00:01:55.970
Nii-san, make sure you do come home.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:02:00.620
Right now, I have a place to come home to.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.410
So I'll come home, no matter what.

00:02:23.590 --> 00:02:26.290
Did he think me an awful mother

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:28.880
for not seeing him off?

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:33.720
I wasn't confident that
I could actually let him go.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.160
If our eyes met,
and I tried to hold him back,

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.560
he probably wouldn't have been able to leave.

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:44.650
Nii-san left with high hopes.

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:47.160
I'm sure it'll be a great trip.

00:02:48.760 --> 00:02:51.330
Yes, you're right.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:55.100
This is something that
you decided for yourselves.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.730
I'm sure Sou-san would've allowed it, too.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.050
"Nasebanaru" to hito wa yuuga

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:08.050
People say, "Where there's 
a will, there's a way"

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.500
Narugamama naseba ii

00:03:08.050 --> 00:03:11.500
But things can just be how they'll be

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:24.190
Nagareru kawa ukabu kobune

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:24.190
A small boat floats along the river

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:28.100
Doko ni yukuno darouka

00:03:24.190 --> 00:03:28.100
I wonder where it's going

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:33.320
Ikisaki nado yosou dekinu

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:33.320
I can't even guess its destination

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:37.270
Sorega omoshiroki koto

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:37.270
But that's why it's so fun

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:46.700
Kokorozashi wa takaku mokuhyou wa hikuku

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:46.700
My intentions are high, but my goals are low

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.780
Aho wo mazerya kekka

00:03:46.890 --> 00:03:51.780
When foolishness gets mixed in

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:58.800
Yukai ni nareru

00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:58.800
Everything will be merry

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.520
Narugamama ni sawagu mama ni

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:05.520
As things will be, as chaotic as they will be

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.220
Toraburu suramo nenryou sa

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:10.220
Even troubles become fuel

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.670
Namikaze tatanai jinsei wa

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.670
A life lived without any strife

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.190
Chotto bakkari tsumaranai

00:04:14.670 --> 00:04:19.190
Can be a bit boring

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:23.860
Okiraku ni gokuraku ni

00:04:19.190 --> 00:04:23.860
Carefree and blissfully

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.440
Kaze ni makasete ikou

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.440
Let's let the wind lead us

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:33.000
Kyou mo bakashite ikou

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:33.000
Let's go trick everyone again today

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.000
<b>Episode Nine
The Various Nidaime</b>

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:40.290
I'm always causing trouble.

00:04:40.290 --> 00:04:43.510
A whole lotta trouble.

00:04:43.510 --> 00:04:46.690
I'm always gonna disturb the peace.

00:04:46.690 --> 00:04:49.990
Always gonna disturb the peace.

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.120
Yasaburo.

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:53.620
Come here for a second.

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:56.360
Akadama-sensei refuses

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:01.860
to be the observer
for the Trick Magister elections.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:05.950
He said he would appoint
another tengu to the position, but...

00:05:06.150 --> 00:05:08.370
I'm sure it'll be Benten-sama.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.170
But that's far too cruel.

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:13.570
He's suggesting we welcome
the human who put Father

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:17.490
into a hot pot and ate him to the banquet
to decide the head of tanuki society.

00:05:17.490 --> 00:05:20.790
Couldn't we just do this without any tengu?

00:05:21.030 --> 00:05:22.410
That's not possible.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.110
The Trick Magister's authority

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:27.890
is based on the agreement of the tanuki world
and the approval of the great tengu.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.080
If we skip the process,

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:33.470
the Trick Magister will just be a figurehead.

00:05:33.790 --> 00:05:35.130
Good grief.

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:37.490
I guess we don't have a choice.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:42.930
Oh, there he is.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.940
Yasaburo's here.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:47.590
Sorry about this, Yasaburo,

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:51.340
but we want to ask for your help
as a tengu expert.

00:05:51.340 --> 00:05:54.910
There you go flattering
me again, Yasaka-san.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:58.420
Shimogamo Yasaburo has arrived.

00:05:58.720 --> 00:06:00.850
Why did you come?

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:02.170
I didn't summon you.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:06.220
I see that you're fussing
and troubling the tanuki again.

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:08.870
Nothing less from the tengu among tengu,

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:11.710
the great Nyoigatake Yakushibo.

00:06:11.710 --> 00:06:15.220
Yasaka Heitaro came crying to me.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:19.590
I'm sure this is some ploy
to drag me out of here.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:21.860
Ah, so you see right through us.

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:22.770
You fool.

00:06:23.620 --> 00:06:26.480
I'm going to have Benten be the observer.

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.990
End of story.

00:06:39.710 --> 00:06:43.310
And another boring day comes to an end.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.970
Why don't you turn on the light?

00:06:46.970 --> 00:06:50.450
Why must I do something like that myself?

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:51.920
Turn it on for me.

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:53.070
No.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:54.890
Please do it yourself.

00:06:59.530 --> 00:07:05.020
Why do you want to make Benten-sama
the observer, Akadama-sensei?

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:12.080
Are you trying to create a <i>fait accompli</i>

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:15.620
by forcibly appointing Benten-sama
as your successor?

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:23.630
I do believe I've stayed here long enough.

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.860
I'll take my leave now.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:40.980
<b>Nyoigatake Yakushibo 
Countermeasure Headquarters</b>

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.980
How did things go?

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.980
I'm out of ideas.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.900
What should we do, Yasaka-san?

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.050
This isn't good.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:48.710
No good at all.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:51.760
What should we do, Yaichiro-kun?

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:53.720
What should we do, indeed.

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:57.160
I have a good idea.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:59.300
I'm sure it's an awful idea.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:01.670
We should ask the Nidaime for help.

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:05.280
If the Nidaime gets involved,
Benten-sama won't be able to do anything.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:07.880
You have a point, but...

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.750
I wonder if the Nidaime would agree.

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:12.760
We don't have anything to lose.

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:14.670
You're right.

00:08:14.670 --> 00:08:17.120
It will be great if this works out.

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:17.890
One moment.

00:08:18.240 --> 00:08:20.860
I can't agree to that.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.760
And why is that?

00:08:22.760 --> 00:08:27.040
A quarrel over succession among tengu
should be left with the tengu.

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:31.620
We should avoid getting caught up
in a tengu quarrel at all costs.

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.440
If we ask for the Nidaime's help,

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:40.030
who knows how enraged 
Akadama-sensei and Benten-sama will be?

00:08:40.030 --> 00:08:43.220
You can just say it was all my idea.

00:08:43.220 --> 00:08:44.330
I'll take responsibility.

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.210
Are you being serious?

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:50.630
A fun thing is a good thing, Yaichiro.

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:52.340
Leave this to me.

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:55.750
Very well.

00:08:55.750 --> 00:08:58.490
Let's leave this to Yasaburo.

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.850
You've got a fine brother, Yaichiro-kun.

00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:04.850
What, Yaichiro? Cheer up.

00:09:04.850 --> 00:09:06.650
Things are about to get interesting.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:09.430
Good, good.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:20.620
Shimogamo Yasaburo has arrived.

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:22.580
Hello.

00:09:25.130 --> 00:09:27.620
My name is Shimogamo Yaichiro.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:32.340
So, what can I do for you today?

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.000
Nothing really.

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.970
Rather, I have a status report.

00:09:37.570 --> 00:09:38.770
Have a seat.

00:09:39.710 --> 00:09:43.250
First, I have some information
about your gun.

00:09:43.250 --> 00:09:44.810
Did you find it?

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:45.820
Yes.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:48.750
A man named Tenmaya had it.

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:54.650
Furthermore, the gun was used to take
the life of Ebisugawa Soun at Arima Onsen.

00:09:55.150 --> 00:09:58.530
I do not like a piece of art
being used to kill tanuki.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:02.360
Tenmaya disappeared that very night,

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:05.370
and I have not had a chance
to recover the gun.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:08.860
This is all my fault.

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:12.310
I regret to say that I have
no way of repaying you.

00:10:12.310 --> 00:10:14.010
What are you talking about?

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:16.720
You've done plenty for me already.

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:20.600
I was able to get my furniture back
because of you.

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:22.890
I am in your debt.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.850
Are you that concerned about debts to tanuki?

00:10:29.230 --> 00:10:32.520
I would be thankful if you would
accept payment as thanks.

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:36.350
Suppose we set the situation
with the German gun aside,

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:38.110
would it still be quite a debt?

00:10:38.650 --> 00:10:39.720
Well, now.

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:42.400
This is starting to reek of tanuki.

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:45.060
I wonder where this conversation is going.

00:10:45.520 --> 00:10:46.950
Why don't we get to the point?

00:10:47.610 --> 00:10:49.620
I beg your pardon,

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:54.380
but could we ask you to be the observer
in the upcoming Trick Magister elections?

00:10:55.080 --> 00:10:57.080
Why don't you ask the man

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:59.940
who could barely be called a tengu

00:10:59.940 --> 00:11:04.390
and lives meagerly in Demachiyanagi
to do that for you?

00:11:04.670 --> 00:11:07.890
Actually... I'm just going to be
upfront about this.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:11.440
We've already asked Akadama-sensei,

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.880
but he's appointed Benten-sama.

00:11:14.280 --> 00:11:18.350
She is a member of the Friday Club,
which eats tanuki hot pots.

00:11:18.350 --> 00:11:20.300
She is not fit to be the observer.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:25.360
That's why we would like you
to be the observer instead.

00:11:25.360 --> 00:11:28.200
Are you asking me to become a tengu?

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.290
Oh, no.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:32.620
We're asking you to become the observer.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:35.540
But the observer is the role of a tengu.

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:41.380
That's just how the tanuki
and tengu societies think it should be,

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:45.130
but there's no reason
to be bound to old traditions.

00:11:45.130 --> 00:11:48.850
We would just like you
to be the observer as the Nidaime.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:50.350
That's all.

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:53.300
"The Nidaime," eh?

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:56.330
Truth be told, it is my older brother's dream

00:11:56.330 --> 00:12:00.820
to follow in our late father's footsteps
and become the Trick Magister.

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:05.620
As his younger brother, I would do anything
I can to make that dream come true.

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:06.320
Hey...

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.650
I see.

00:12:08.190 --> 00:12:10.410
Following in your father's footsteps...

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:13.820
So you want to follow the same path he did?

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:15.330
Yes.

00:12:15.330 --> 00:12:18.060
All my life, I have searched
for a different path.

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:22.320
In other words, I have no intention
of becoming a tengu or succeeding him.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:23.300
And...

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:27.270
I don't want to have to clean up
after that senile old fool's messes.

00:12:27.270 --> 00:12:30.360
I see. Well, this is a problem.

00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:33.310
I can never let my guard down around you.

00:12:34.780 --> 00:12:37.440
I'm not that impressive.

00:12:37.440 --> 00:12:40.820
You were spying on me the other day
at Kiyomizu-dera, weren't you?

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:41.770
Spying?!

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:46.220
Oh, you knew? But I meant no harm.

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:49.200
I was just curious.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:51.590
Did that old man put you up to it?

00:12:51.590 --> 00:12:55.080
I'd rather not comment on that.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:59.630
To have a tanuki minion track his lover...

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:01.510
It's so absurd that I have no words.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:03.120
The epitome of aged degradation.

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:07.620
The mistake that the old man is
worried about would never happen.

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:11.850
The fact that he would even
consider it is truly insulting.

00:13:12.390 --> 00:13:16.580
You must really hate Benten-sama.

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:20.200
I don't hate her. I loathe her.

00:13:21.370 --> 00:13:24.950
I encountered her once in England.

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:30.660
Despite loathing her,
you are quite kind to Benten-sama.

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:33.040
What are you talking about?

00:13:33.360 --> 00:13:35.250
I have no kindness for her.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:39.800
But you were being rather cordial with her.

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:43.800
Nonsense! My friend,
you are grossly mistaken.

00:13:44.240 --> 00:13:45.840
I'm not so sure about that.

00:13:45.840 --> 00:13:49.180
I simply thought that
she is not fit to be a tengu.

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:56.090
At this rate, Benten-sama will become
the new Nyoigatake Yakushibo.

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:58.230
Should such a thing be allowed?

00:13:58.230 --> 00:14:03.020
We have no other choice
but to depend on you to stop Benten-sama.

00:14:03.520 --> 00:14:07.420
I beg of you to help us tanuki.

00:14:07.420 --> 00:14:09.740
I humbly implore you.

00:14:10.150 --> 00:14:12.950
Please stop using such uncouth methods.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:15.750
We won't stop until you accept.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.040
All right, fine.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:22.500
Tell your fellow tanuki

00:14:22.940 --> 00:14:25.220
that I will act as observer.

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:31.010
<b>Nidaime's Mansion</b>

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:31.010
<b>Nishizaki Genemon Shoten</b>

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:31.010
<b>Rokkaku-do</b>

00:14:28.010 --> 00:14:31.010
<b>Coffee Tsutaya</b>

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:33.260
Thank you very much.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.390
We're now even, Yasaburo-kun.

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:21.970
This is a dangerous place
for you to be, miss.

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:24.930
I'm fine,

00:15:26.520 --> 00:15:28.140
so please leave me alone.

00:15:49.800 --> 00:15:52.920
I'm surprised you could
finish two servings, Yaichiro.

00:15:53.310 --> 00:15:57.040
The Trick Magister must
have plenty of energy.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:16:00.600
I won't be able to last the long haul
on energy drinks alone.

00:16:00.600 --> 00:16:03.940
There is a need to eat
nutritious foods regularly.

00:16:04.270 --> 00:16:07.320
It's a good thing to eat
many delicious things.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:09.940
But...

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:13.040
This hamburg steak looks
almost like a tanuki.

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:16.510
Please don't say such awful things, Mother.

00:16:21.390 --> 00:16:22.210
Oh?

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:24.880
You're being rather quiet.

00:16:25.310 --> 00:16:27.460
Well, hello there, Yasaburo-dono.

00:16:27.460 --> 00:16:32.220
I'm sure Hesoishi-sama is quite pleased
with the fine weather we're having.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:34.360
It's wonderful.

00:16:34.360 --> 00:16:36.250
Wonderful, indeed.

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:37.180
Namu, namu.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:41.640
Did you two eat something strange?

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.090
What are you saying?

00:16:43.090 --> 00:16:46.010
We are working hard not
to be fools any longer.

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:48.330
Our brother, Kureichiro, teaches us,

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:51.650
and we train day and night.

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:55.620
My older brother and I have
become as pleasant as chilled,

00:16:55.620 --> 00:16:57.480
soft and fluffy steamed cakes.

00:16:57.480 --> 00:17:00.460
We recommend the path of Buddha
to you as well, Yasaburo-dono.

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.660
The age of fools has passed.

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:06.500
I see. I wish you two luck.

00:17:06.500 --> 00:17:07.630
I'm rooting for you.

00:17:08.320 --> 00:17:09.260
Close the gates.

00:17:12.250 --> 00:17:14.320
Please settle down.

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:17.390
We shall now begin our meeting.

00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.250
But before we proceed,

00:17:19.250 --> 00:17:23.620
we have gratefully received
some words from Hesoishi-sama.

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:28.510
I shall now read them,
so I ask for your attention.

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:37.240
"When you catch a cold,
warm your feet and chill your head.

00:17:37.240 --> 00:17:39.000
Then you won't need a doctor.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:42.830
Drinking warm water with honey
and ginger is super awesome, too."

00:17:43.440 --> 00:17:44.660
That is all.

00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:54.550
Now, Yaichiro-kun, who is
our Trick Magister candidate,

00:17:54.550 --> 00:17:57.890
is a very promising tanuki
for the new generation.

00:17:57.890 --> 00:17:59.540
Huzzah! Our new hope!

00:17:59.540 --> 00:18:00.550
Nidaime!

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:04.520
Kureichiro-kun will give a speech
in support of our candidate.

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:08.760
He now leads the Ebisugawa clan
after his late father's passing

00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:11.590
and is another promising tanuki
for the new generation.

00:18:12.090 --> 00:18:15.940
Now then, Kureichiro-kun, if you would.

00:18:18.210 --> 00:18:22.660
I am Ebisugawa Soun's eldest son,
Ebisugawa Kureichiro.

00:18:22.920 --> 00:18:28.280
Though my father brought the
Trick Denki Bran factory into modernity,

00:18:28.280 --> 00:18:32.670
his wretched deeds
later in life cannot be forgotten.

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:38.260
Even so, Yaichiro-kun has offered
to let bygones be bygones

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.550
and asked that we live in peace together.

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:44.650
The Ebisugawa family will support
the new Trick Magister.

00:18:44.650 --> 00:18:48.890
We will do everything in our power
to bring a bright future to the tanuki world.

00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:53.220
Thank you, Kureichiro.

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:54.370
Thank you.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.060
Huzzah! The new generation!

00:18:56.060 --> 00:18:58.070
The 21st century!

00:18:58.070 --> 00:19:01.440
The elders will have their meeting

00:19:01.440 --> 00:19:05.060
on the night of December 26th
to discuss this further.

00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:07.530
Next, we have another announcement.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:12.260
It has been decided that the Nidaime
will fill the role of the observer

00:19:12.260 --> 00:19:17.810
of the election of the Trick Magister,
the head of tanuki society.

00:19:18.210 --> 00:19:20.300
I doubt there are any objections.

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:21.660
Objection.

00:19:28.220 --> 00:19:31.350
B-Benten-sama has arrived!

00:19:35.440 --> 00:19:40.470
My master ordered me to be
the observer of the tanuki elections,

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:43.240
but apparently, I'm not welcome here.

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:46.050
Oh, is that so?

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:48.750
It appears that there may be
a misunderstanding.

00:19:48.930 --> 00:19:53.500
I don't mind if that wannabe-Brit
wants to take over, though.

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:55.500
Thank you for your understanding.

00:19:55.690 --> 00:20:01.380
But I would like to know how
such a misunderstanding came to pass.

00:20:01.690 --> 00:20:06.220
I wonder if you tanuki don't like
the idea of my becoming the observer.

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:09.390
Oh, no. It's nothing like that.

00:20:09.390 --> 00:20:10.460
It's fine.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:13.920
After all, I am a woman
who eats tanuki hot pots.

00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:16.770
I can understand how you tanuki feel.

00:20:17.270 --> 00:20:20.240
But despite understanding
how you feel, I'll eat you anyway.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.620
I am human, after all.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:26.030
I can make all the tanuki hot pots I want.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:38.090
Oh, my.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:42.500
I didn't know you were
hiding there, Yasaburo.

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:46.200
I'm sure this is all your doing.

00:20:46.200 --> 00:20:48.470
I'm surprised you were able to persuade him.

00:20:48.710 --> 00:20:51.920
I haven't the slightest idea
what you're talking about.

00:20:51.920 --> 00:20:52.900
You're lying.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:54.980
Indeed, I am. I'm very sorry.

00:20:55.190 --> 00:20:56.690
Such a foolish tanuki.

00:20:56.900 --> 00:21:00.940
You know me very well, Benten-sama.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:05.680
The fool's blood that runs within me
makes me do peculiar things.

00:21:05.680 --> 00:21:07.950
I'm not even sure what I want to do.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.640
Betraying Akadama-sensei, betraying you,

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:13.420
coercing the Nidaime...

00:21:11.640 --> 00:21:14.040
I hate that man.

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:19.290
The Nidaime mentioned that
he hates you, too, Benten-sama.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:21.040
And what about you?

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:23.300
Do you like him or me?

00:21:23.620 --> 00:21:26.050
I have the utmost respect 
for both of you as tengu—

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:46.550
<i>My grandmother told me to make sure
to cause some trouble and keep things fun.</i>

00:21:47.020 --> 00:21:48.610
<i>Following those words,</i>

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:51.920
<i>I boldly said, "Leave it to me!"</i>

00:21:52.490 --> 00:21:56.460
<i>But this scheme was too great a gamble</i>

00:21:56.460 --> 00:21:58.950
<i>for a mere tanuki.</i>

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:09.300
Tsuki wo medetewa toki ni wa nusunde

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:09.300
While gazing lovingly at the 
moon, at times, she steals it

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:14.140
Kimagure na kanojo wa ah

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:14.140
Whimsical as she may be, ah

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:18.640
Kawabe de hitori hoho ni namida

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:18.640
As she stands by the riverside 
alone, secretly her tears

00:22:18.640 --> 00:22:22.980
Utsukushiku tayutau

00:22:18.640 --> 00:22:22.980
Quiver beautifully upon her cheeks

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:34.740
Boku no te tori nagara 
kokoro wa dokoka ni ukabu

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:34.740
She takes my hand, as her 
heart floats away somewhere

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:39.240
Kasaneta te ni wa mada nukumori

00:22:34.740 --> 00:22:39.240
I still feel that warmth from her held hand

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:43.630
Setsunai yume no sono ato saki

00:22:39.240 --> 00:22:43.630
Somewhere beyond this sentimental dream

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:53.260
Demo kimi no me wa harukana 
mirai wo miteitane

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:53.260
But you were already looking 
far into the future

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:57.920
Zutto zutto oikaketayo

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:57.920
I always chased after you

00:22:57.920 --> 00:23:02.270
Kimi ga kizutsuku toki mo

00:22:57.920 --> 00:23:02.270
Even when you were hurt

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:11.670
Sotto mabuta ni yakitsuita kimi no sugata ni

00:23:02.270 --> 00:23:11.670
The vision of you that's 
softly imprinted on my eyes

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:16.570
Ima mata tooku e to ah

00:23:11.670 --> 00:23:16.570
Once again, you fly far away, ah

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:28.940
Tondeiku kimi wa hora Kanata no hito

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:28.940
You are a person far beyond

00:23:30.760 --> 00:23:33.010
Apparently, there aren't
any foxes in Shikoku.

00:23:33.390 --> 00:23:36.180
Apparently, Kobo Daishi chased
them all out, or something.

00:23:36.520 --> 00:23:40.430
On that note, I wonder how I'm
supposed to get out of Shikoku.

00:23:37.520 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Episode Ten
The Day the Trick Magister is Chosen</b>
